-- title:
--   Regularity of R/(ivarpi) for a retraction onto a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a regular local ring, and let $A$ be a commutative ring which is a domain and a discrete valuation ring. Let $i\colon A\to R$ and $s\colon R\to A$ be ring homomorphisms such that $s$ is surjective and $s\circ i$ is the identity of $A$, so that $i$ is a section of the retraction $s$, and let $\varpi\in A$ be irreducible. The conclusion asserts the existence of a proof that the quotient $R/(i\varpi)$, by the ideal generated by the single element $i\varpi$, is again a regular local ring, together with, relative to that regularity, two numerical statements: first, the minimal number of generators of the maximal ideal of $R/(i\varpi)$, in the sense of `Ideal.spanFinrank`, plus one equals the minimal number of generators of the maximal ideal of $R$; second, the Krull dimension of $R/(i\varpi)$ plus one equals the Krull dimension of $R$, the equality being of elements of the ordered monoid in which `ringKrullDim` takes its values.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a section through a regular point cuts the special fibre in a regular point of one lower dimension: dividing a regular local ring by a uniformiser of a discrete valuation subring that is split off by a surjection preserves regularity and drops both embedding dimension and Krull dimension by one. It is used in the proof that the local rings arising from formally smooth, formally unramified situations over Henselian local rings are regular.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton_map_of_leftInverse_of_irreducible.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
